.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt BQ27220 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bq27220
.Nd TI BQ27220 battery fuel gauge
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "bq27220g* at iic?"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver attaches to a device-tree node compatible with
.Qq ti,bq27220
and exposes read-only measurements through
.Xr sysmon_envsys 9 .
The driver does not configure gauge data memory, chemistry parameters, or
one-time-programmable storage.
.Pp
The following sensors are available through
.Xr envstat 8 :
.Bl -tag -width "battery charge"
.It battery voltage
Cell-pack voltage, in volts.
.It battery current
Signed current, in amperes; positive values indicate current into the battery.
.It gauge temperature
The gauge's
.Sy Temperature()
reading, in degrees Celsius as presented by envsys.
The chip's configuration determines whether this reading comes from an
external thermistor, its internal sensor, or a host-written value.
.It battery charge
State of charge, as a percentage.
.El
.Pp
Read errors and out-of-range readings mark the affected sensor invalid.
.Sh DEVICE TREE
.Bl -tag -width "compatible"
.It compatible
.Qq ti,bq27220
.It reg
I2C address.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr envsys 4 ,
.Xr envstat 8 ,
.Xr sysmon_envsys 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in EmberBSD 11.
.Sh AUTHORS
The driver was written for EmberBSD.
